                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "4d02b90a-dc33-41ce-9b13-4db271114d15",
                        "entry_id": "09527c9c-80d8-3961-bddb-7932f6c1d556",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "ribibes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1ebfe887-2ea1-3b1f-b861-60f5f0069691",
                        "entry_id": "09527c9c-80d8-3961-bddb-7932f6c1d556",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A kind of stringed instrument; a rebec or an instrument similar to it."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "372a52b6-f101-4fd3-851e-bdc769661f73",
                                "sense_id": "1ebfe887-2ea1-3b1f-b861-60f5f0069691",
                                "text": "Well, my friend, and where is your ribibe, or such like instrument, belonging to a minstrel?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d804f2e8-298a-4c3a-8b4c-ce39916e7d27",
                                "sense_id": "1ebfe887-2ea1-3b1f-b861-60f5f0069691",
                                "text": "\"The tones of lutes and ribibes [translating German Ribeben]\nI have right masterly and fine As ordered by imperial might."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0b34d68c-760f-44ae-ae40-f06b1d5b2041",
                                "sense_id": "1ebfe887-2ea1-3b1f-b861-60f5f0069691",
                                "text": "The tone of the rubebe was similar to that of the lower register of the modern viola. As it possessed but two strings, however, its range was necessarily limited."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bea59820-6297-4718-a763-dcab33eac29f",
                                "sense_id": "1ebfe887-2ea1-3b1f-b861-60f5f0069691",
                                "text": "The Rybybe is well portrayed among the Norman carvings of the twelfth century which adorn the south doorway of Barfreston Church in Kent (Plate XV)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "604440e2-cd56-42be-a17f-d306d7d5c2c6",
                                "sense_id": "1ebfe887-2ea1-3b1f-b861-60f5f0069691",
                                "text": "Over the high-altar at Gloucester the bosses, which are foliated in the rest of the choir, represent angel-musicians, whose varied orchestra would have out-rivalled that of Nebuchadnezzar the King; harp, hutchet and psaltery; lute, clarion, shawm; bag-pipe, ribibe, gittern; bozine, symphony, cymbals; organ, tabor and timbrel, the very names ring in one's ears like the stately cadences of celestial music."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c6763d43-316a-4fd9-897f-0b15fdf944cd",
                                "sense_id": "1ebfe887-2ea1-3b1f-b861-60f5f0069691",
                                "text": "The rebec or ribibe, a favourite instrument with Chaucer, may be counted as one of the precursors of our violin."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "25c6e84c-ed34-4363-9e71-b7e6c52e472f",
                                "sense_id": "1ebfe887-2ea1-3b1f-b861-60f5f0069691",
                                "text": "The Persian hunting scene, the Arabian ribibi. Here, that is, in Janequin we find ground for one of the basic dissociations of music."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a5b11aa5-5f9a-3310-960d-bc4b8b2af52d",
                        "entry_id": "09527c9c-80d8-3961-bddb-7932f6c1d556",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An old woman."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "derogatory",
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a14cad46-9c3e-38ed-bbea-14ac4db3876c",
                        "entry_id": "09527c9c-80d8-3961-bddb-7932f6c1d556",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A bawd; a prostitute."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3269f86d-9937-411c-be6d-84fa8b31d864",
                                "sense_id": "a14cad46-9c3e-38ed-bbea-14ac4db3876c",
                                "text": "Or some good ribibe about Kentish Town or Hogsden, you would hang now for a witch"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
